  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Quadratic expressions appear frequently on the EST I — in standard, vertex, and factored forms. Knowing how to move between forms and when to use each is a key skill.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Quadratic forms",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Standard: \\( ax^2+bx+c \\). Vertex: \\( a(x-h)^2+k \\) with vertex at \\( (h,k) \\). Factored: \\( a(x-r_1)(x-r_2) \\) with roots \\( r_1, r_2 \\). Quadratic formula: \\( x=\\dfrac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a} \\). Discriminant \\( \\Delta = b^2-4ac \\): positive → two real roots, zero → one root, negative → no real roots.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Parabola in vertex form",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "estParabCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A parabola y equals a times x minus h squared plus k, with adjustable a, h, and k",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
